  "description": {
    "sub_id3": null,
    "sub_name": "低軌衛星通訊網路",
    "sub_ename": "LOW EARTH ORBIT SATELLITE COMMUNICATION NETWORKS",
    "describe_ch": "本課程介紹低軌衛星通訊網路的基本概念、系統架構與應用，內容涵蓋衛星軌道設計、星座配置、實體層與天線技術、媒體存取控制、網路與傳輸層協定，以及與地面網路及5G/6G NTN技術之整合。課程結合理論與實作，透過 MATLAB 進行衛星下鏈路模擬、軌道可視化、波束追蹤與 DVB-S2(X) 系統實驗，並利用 Ubuntu 平台完成端對端傳輸與地面站排程實作。課程最後探討永續性、太空安全與資安議題，培養學生低軌衛星通訊設計與實務能力。",
    "describe_eh": "This course provides an introduction to Low Earth Orbit (LEO) satellite communication networks, covering fundamental concepts, system architecture, and practical applications. Topics include satellite orbit design, constellation configuration, physical layer and antenna technologies, medium access control, network and transport layer protocols, as well as the integration of satellite systems with terrestrial networks and emerging 5G/6G Non-Terrestrial Networks (NTN). The course combines theory with hands-on practice through MATLAB-based experiments such as downlink communication simulation, orbit visualization, beam tracking, and DVB-S2(X) system implementation. Additionally, students will work with Ubuntu platforms to conduct end-to-end transmission and ground station scheduling. The course concludes with discussions on sustainability, space safety, and cybersecurity, equipping students with both theoretical knowledge and practical skills for LEO satellite communication system design and implementation.",
    "pre_subname": "",
    "pre_sub_id3": null,
    "pre_sub_ename": "",
